From da2d76749a9052e315b515f517c84df379cca17e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malard <malard@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:42:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [peripherals][CPeripherals] Skip a mapping setting without a
 key

GetSettingsFromMappingsFile skipped a <setting> with no key attribute by
continuing the loop before moving to the next element, so it read the
same element for ever. One keyless entry in a peripheral mappings file
hung the thread loading it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 46017143b506f9462d9973f2c805392d38e3baed)
---
 cmake/treedata/common/tests.txt               |  1 +
 xbmc/peripherals/Peripherals.cpp              |  3 +
 xbmc/peripherals/Peripherals.h                |  2 +
 xbmc/peripherals/test/CMakeLists.txt          |  3 +
 .../test/TestPeripheralMappings.cpp           | 66 +++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 75 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/peripherals/test/CMakeLists.txt
 create mode 100644 xbmc/peripherals/test/TestPeripheralMappings.cpp

